{
 "logline": "A lone rider begs at the gate and counts the hours to dawn. Frost creeps over burning desert sand, the knocks come in threes, and the one thing that never breathes is the man asking to be let in.",
 "motif": "Three knocks, frost on warm sand, and a countdown. Every film ends on a number (7, 6, 5, 4 hours, then 2 and 1 fires, then 8). Each beacon that lights doubles as a menu-unlock beat. The clue is breath: the champion's breath smokes, the rider's never does.",
 "twist": "The rider is not fleeing the dead, he is leading them. Dawn is his word for the eighth beacon, the moment the host reaches the south. Fair-play clues: no hoofbeats (F0), the champion asks to see his breath (F0), a warm-waxed letter says not to answer (F1), a shape standing too still and the one breath that does not smoke (F3). F4 pays them off and cuts to the Night King.",
 "notes": "Validated: all scene ids, sfx keys and caption kinds allowed; every caption <= 8 words, hold >= 1.6, at+hold <= shot d, never more than 2 visible at once; tutorial_lines has 13 entries (2 and 6 blank, {SKILL} in 5, line 12 without castle/menu). Fix applied: F6 title card now '1 FIRE' (was '1 HOUR') to match the hours-to-fires switch in F4. Seconds per film: F0 42.0 s / 11 shots (title at 34.2 s = 81%); F1 21.6 s / 6 shots; F2 12.8 s / 4 shots; F3 13.4 s / 4 shots; F4 30.0 s / 8 shots; F5 8.2 s / 3 shots; F6 8.2 s / 3 shots; F7 8.4 s / 3 shots.",
